        "instagram": null,
        "inmate_number": null,
        "awaiting_trial": 0,
        "created_at": "2026-10-01 11:57:00",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-12 19:17:32",
        "slug": "hudson-austin",
        "body": "<h2>U.S. military custody</h2><p>Amnesty International records arrest in late October 1983 and nine to twelve days of U.S. detention, followed by handover to Grenadian and Caribbean Peacekeeping Force authorities around November 5, 1983. Individual exact endpoints have not been established. The case date is stored with month precision. The transfer was not freedom from confinement, so it is not recorded as a release date. No single day count is inferred from the reported range.</p><h2>Subsequent Grenadian imprisonment</h2><p>Associated Press reports actual release from Richmond Hill Prison on December 18, 2008.</p><p>The years spent in Richmond Hill Prison after handover are distinct from the U.S. military detention. They are described here and are not counted as years in U.S. custody.</p><h2>U.S. military custody ended by transfer</h2><p><a href='https://www.amnesty.org/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/amr320012003en.pdf#page=6'>Amnesty International's original 2003 report, page 6</a>, dates transfer from U.S. military detention to Grenadian and Caribbean Peacekeeping Force custody to on or around November 5, 1983. Page 2 identifies all seventeen members individually. Both original pages were rendered and visually reviewed. The U.S. case endpoint is therefore November 1983 at month precision, not an exact November 5 day and not release to freedom. Later Grenadian custody, court proceedings and actual release must remain distinct.</p>",
        "under_review": 0,
        "imprisoned_or_exiled": 0,
        "date_precision": "{\"birthdate\":\"year\"}",
        "minor_case": 0
